          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto has built three AI agents, plus a few practices he uses to build and run them:\n\n1. **Fraud Detection Agent** (offline evals, nearing deployment): For an online event ticketing platform, it reviews new events and organizers and recommends approve, reject, or request-info for a human admin. In offline evals (31 cases), the chosen model, Claude Haiku 4.5, reached 86% accuracy and let 1% of fraud through, versus 71% and 8% for a local 9B model. Stack: TypeScript, PostgreSQL, GCP.\n2. **Organizer Support Agent** (coming soon, not yet built): Would answer organizers' questions about sales, payouts and setup by pulling live data from PostgreSQL and the payments API. Stack: TypeScript, tool calling, MCP, PostgreSQL.\n3. **Portfolio Agent** (personal project): The agent on this site that answers questions about Alberto's experience and projects. It is also exposed as an MCP server. Stack: TypeScript, Claude, MCP.\n\nWould you like more detail on any of these, or on how he evaluates agents?",
